@startuml mf-01-pickup
' SRS Section II.1.2.1 — Main Workflow: Pickup
' Continues in mf-02a-reserve-aim.puml
' The tail of this flow changed with the dynamic drop-off: the pick-up no longer
' hands over to an approach order (TO2); WES reserves a concrete drop-off slot
' and aims the drop-off order (TO3) straight at it.
' Business-level vocabulary only; implementation detail belongs in the SDS.
' Render: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng mf-01-pickup.puml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam swimlaneWidth 260
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #000000
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #7ACFF4
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #000000
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #7ACFF4
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #7ACFF4
skinparam NoteBorderColor #000000

|Scanner|
|WES|
|FMS (openTCS)|
|AGV|

|Scanner|
start
:Create cargo;
note right: source point\n+ destination zone

|WES|
:Validate request\n(source point, drop-off zone);
if (Valid?) then (No)
  :Request reject;
  stop
else (Yes)
endif
:Check pickup lane safety;
if (A vehicle is already ordered\ndeeper into the same lane?) then (Yes)
  :Reject request;
  stop
else (No)
endif
:Withdraw the orders of deeper tasks\nthat have not set off yet -> BLOCKED;
:Create Cargo and Task -> CREATED;
:Debounce 1.5s;
:Release Engine: check in-lane dependency\n(outer cargo goes before inner);
if (Blocked by an outer cargo?) then (Yes)
  :Task -> BLOCKED until the\nouter cargo leaves its source;
  stop
else (No)
endif
:Task -> READY_TO_ASSIGN;
:Assignment Engine Hungarian\nover distance and battery cost;
if (A suitable free vehicle?) then (No)
  :Tasks wait for the\nnext dispatch cycle;
  stop
else (Yes)
endif
:Call openTCS to create TO1\n(intendedVehicle = matched AGV);
:Task -> PICKING_UP;

|FMS (openTCS)|
:Receive TO1, route the vehicle\nto the pickup location;
:Send the order to the AGV;

|AGV|
:Drive -> Load cargo -> Report finished;

|FMS (openTCS)|
:Call back TO1 FINISHED to WES;

|WES|
:Reserve a concrete drop-off slot\nin the destination zone (BR-11);
:Call openTCS to create TO3\n(DROP_OFF aimed at the reserved slot);
:Task -> DELIVERING (continues in MF-02);
stop

@enduml
